# SSH signing keys allowed to sign lane commits.
#
# Git only checks SSH signatures when gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile points at a
# file like this one. Without it, `git verify-commit` fails on every commit and
# `git log --show-signature` reports "No signature", even when the commits are
# signed. scripts/verify-signatures.sh points Git at this file itself, so
# shipping and tagging do not depend on a global Git setting.
#
# Format: <principal> <key type> <base64 key>
# The principal must equal the committer email on the commit.
#
# To add a machine, append its public signing key:
#   ssh-keygen -lf ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_signing.pub   # check the fingerprint first
# then run scripts/verify-signatures.sh to confirm the whole range verifies.

# MacBook signing key (SHA256:zoaud/nesPC4bFgVuudDCE6Lb1tT1+AMLEIPqYfjDqQ)
ducpham1912@gmail.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDsmduMa356rifMgDPJe6ZHthW0Tcbl2q2QODdP19X6N

